Tether Moves 951 BTC Worth $70.5M Into Reserves As Holdings Near 97,141 BTC

@tether transferred 951 $BTC valued at roughly $70.5 million from a Bitfinex hot wallet into a reserve address tied to its treasury operations, Arkham data shows. The move continues the company's quarterly Bitcoin accumulation under a 2023 policy that allocates 15% of net realized profits to BTC purchases, converting stablecoin issuance revenue into a growing balance sheet position.

Reserve addresses attributed to Tether now hold approximately 97,141 BTC, placing the stablecoin issuer among the largest private corporate Bitcoin holders globally. The accumulation strategy ties acquisition size directly to $USDT business revenue, making each cycle a steady source of Bitcoin demand that pulls coins out of exchange liquidity into long-term custody.

